WEBVTT

00:00:32.907 --> 00:00:34.743
Look out!

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.836
That's how you sullied
the name of the Heaven's Blades and

00:00:44.836 --> 00:00:48.757
were expelled, yet live complacently,
as if it meant nothing?

00:00:56.014 --> 00:00:57.223
Heaven's Blades?

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.725
Yes!

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:02.979
Though a Keeper of the Heaven's Blade,
that man brought shame to his sword!

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:04.481
What?

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:07.067
He entered underground
tournaments for money...

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:10.945
and was expelled from Glendan.
That is the nature of that man...

00:01:10.945 --> 00:01:13.573
Layfon Alseif!

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:17.160
<i>Leerin.</i>..

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:21.456
<i>That I can be here like</i>
<i>this at all is thanks to you.</i>

00:01:21.456 --> 00:01:25.794
<i>I think it's because you were</i>
<i>there for me during my past in Glendan</i>

00:01:25.794 --> 00:01:30.006
<i>that I didn't end up completely</i>
<i>rejecting the military arts.</i>

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:35.303
<i>But because of that,</i>
<i>my past can't simply disappear.</i>

00:01:35.303 --> 00:01:37.722
<i>The mistake I made with the military arts</i>...

00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:40.433
<i>If I continued down this path,</i>

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.978
<i>I know it will become</i>
<i>a piercing, inescapable hardship.</i>

00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:45.605
Stop!

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:49.943
<i>But I want to believe it will work out somehow.</i>

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.238
<i>I want you to believe that, too.</i>

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:57.075
<i>That's all I can say for now.</i>

00:01:57.075 --> 00:02:00.412
<i>Wishing you the greatest of luck going forward.</i>

00:02:00.412 --> 00:02:05.542
<i>To Leerin Marfes. From Layfon Alseif.</i>

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:12.090
<i>Brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.593
<i>So we can go somewhere with the dite</i>

00:02:15.593 --> 00:02:23.018
<i>Keep hope alive, now we</i>
<i>wanna find the new world</i>

00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:28.773
<i>Chizu o ushinatte samayotteiru machi</i>

00:02:28.773 --> 00:02:32.235
<i>Owariyuku sekai demo</i>

00:02:32.235 --> 00:02:38.950
<i>Karada no oku de hashiru no o yamenai inochi o</i>
<i>kikasete</i>

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.245
<i>Tayasanai hikari o tozasanai hitomi ni</i>

00:02:42.245 --> 00:02:45.623
<i>Kawaitemo yakitsuketa</i>

00:02:45.623 --> 00:02:52.255
<i>Kizutsuku koto mo naku te ni</i>
<i>suru mono nante nanimo shinjinai</i>

00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:58.136
<i>Dareka ni mukatta hitosuji no omoi wa</i>

00:02:58.136 --> 00:03:06.019
<i>Yoake no you ni hagane no yami o kirisaku</i>

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:10.357
<i>Itsuka brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:03:10.357 --> 00:03:14.027
<i>Dakara tsuyoku kaeru</i>

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:19.991
<i>Kasaneta chikara mo inori mo</i>

00:03:19.991 --> 00:03:23.661
<i>Kousa suru mirai, kakaeta negai</i>

00:03:23.661 --> 00:03:27.082
<i>Dare no te ni mo watasenai</i>

00:03:27.082 --> 00:03:28.625
<i>Just tough and alive</i>

00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:33.630
<i>Kokoro o tsuraneru</i>

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:38.593
Sorry to make you always do this.

00:03:38.593 --> 00:03:41.346
Not at all. You've gotten
more students again, haven't you?

00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:44.140
Yes. Two last month.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:48.436
I'm glad! It looks like things
will work out somehow.

00:03:48.436 --> 00:03:51.690
Oh, did you write a response
to that letter from the authorities?

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:52.774
Nope.

00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:54.275
I swear...

00:03:54.275 --> 00:03:57.195
They'll get mad at you
again if you don't respond.

00:03:57.195 --> 00:03:58.238
Yeah.

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.865
Father, you really aren't concerned

00:04:00.865 --> 00:04:03.743
with anything but the military arts, are you?

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:08.373
Leerin, have you gone
by to visit the orphanage?

00:04:08.373 --> 00:04:09.582
Why?

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:13.128
I was thinking the time would be about right.

00:04:13.128 --> 00:04:14.379
I have my own reasons,

00:04:14.379 --> 00:04:18.675
but you have lots of
good friends there, don't you?

00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:20.719
I'll talk to them.

00:04:20.719 --> 00:04:25.515
You can't do that. Because
I chose to stay friends with Layfon.

00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:26.683
But...

00:04:26.683 --> 00:04:30.228
It's because of Layfon
that you quit the orphanage.

00:04:30.228 --> 00:04:33.231
And so did I, having defended him.

00:04:33.231 --> 00:04:35.859
I want to make that point very clear...

00:04:35.859 --> 00:04:37.861
For Layfon's sake as well.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:40.780
You always make that face

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.824
when no matter what I say,
you won't change your mind.

00:04:42.824 --> 00:04:44.451
Exactly!

00:04:45.535 --> 00:04:49.122
Besides, I have a friend in the school dorm.

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:52.250
She's strange but sort of fun...

00:04:57.005 --> 00:04:58.631
Father?

00:05:06.181 --> 00:05:08.016
It's gone, eh?

00:05:08.933 --> 00:05:10.185
What is?

00:05:10.185 --> 00:05:14.481
I don't know.
It's as if it were human yet not human.

00:05:14.481 --> 00:05:18.568
But that presence... Somewhere before, I've...

00:05:21.404 --> 00:05:24.908
"The Right to be a Heaven's Blade"

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:28.036
Well? Nothing out of the ordinary?

00:05:28.036 --> 00:05:29.996
No, sir. No problems with any of these values.

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:31.831
Ah. Roger that.

00:05:36.378 --> 00:05:38.171
Gor, you idiot.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:44.135
I'm very sorry for getting upset.
I hold no animosity toward the 17th.

00:05:44.135 --> 00:05:46.971
I don't want you to get the wrong impression.

00:05:46.971 --> 00:05:50.058
You mentioned "Heaven's Blades."

00:05:50.058 --> 00:05:54.979
Yes. They are keepers of special blades,
just twelve of which exist in the whole world,

00:05:54.979 --> 00:05:58.066
and that only those sanctioned
by Glendan's royal family may wield.

00:05:58.066 --> 00:05:59.984
They are the most powerful of military artists.

00:05:59.984 --> 00:06:01.486
Layfon was one?

00:06:01.486 --> 00:06:05.490
If you don't believe me,
try asking him yourself.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:06.783
Wait.

00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:09.119
So that's what you can't forgive?

00:06:09.119 --> 00:06:13.081
That Layfon acted improperly
while a Keeper of the Heaven's Blade?

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:18.545
I'm not as pure-spirited as that.
My anger is purely personal.

00:06:19.754 --> 00:06:23.049
Gahard Barehn. He was a senior student.

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:24.676
Gahard?

00:06:24.676 --> 00:06:28.304
Layfon disabled Gahard-<i>san </i>for life...

00:06:28.304 --> 00:06:32.100
To hide that he was competing
in underground tournaments.

00:06:32.851 --> 00:06:35.061
I won't let my feelings affect the mission.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:40.900
But I'd like you to try to keep
us apart as much as possible.

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.490
No luck over here either.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.702
If the contaminoids got
in through the upper section,

00:06:50.702 --> 00:06:53.705
the civilians should have escaped downward.

00:06:53.705 --> 00:06:56.875
It could be faster to begin
searching the lowest level.

00:06:56.875 --> 00:06:58.710
Still, it's strange.

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:02.589
Not only are there no survivors,
there isn't a single body.

00:07:02.589 --> 00:07:04.883
Maybe the contaminoids
were hungrier than usual

00:07:04.883 --> 00:07:07.427
and gobbled 'em all up at once, huh?

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:12.057
No, even if that were the case,
there should be <i>some </i>remains.

00:07:12.057 --> 00:07:15.143
Remains, huh?

00:07:15.143 --> 00:07:17.687
Yes. I've seen it several times before.

00:07:17.687 --> 00:07:23.735
Ah. 'Cause you're a straight-outta-Glendan,
<i>super </i>battle veteran, huh?

00:07:24.903 --> 00:07:27.030
Don't go lookin' all scary!

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.239
It was just a joke.

00:07:28.239 --> 00:07:30.992
No, it's the truth.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:35.372
Painfully honest, aren't you?

00:07:36.081 --> 00:07:37.207
Layfon!

00:07:37.207 --> 00:07:38.124
Ma'am!

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:39.292
You have a moment?

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:40.919
Ma'am.

00:07:45.173 --> 00:07:49.010
And the in-fighting begins, huh?

00:07:51.554 --> 00:07:55.392
You're a friggin' idiot!
I'm not gonna fall for the same thing twi--

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.313
Did we hit something?

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:01.940
Dunno.

00:08:05.819 --> 00:08:07.445
Monkey.

00:08:15.078 --> 00:08:17.622
That's unexpected, starting off with the judge.

00:08:17.622 --> 00:08:20.125
Someone else involved with that

00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:22.752
Heaven's Blade qualifying match, eh?

00:08:22.752 --> 00:08:25.630
Could he have unexpectedly
retained awareness?

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:26.881
That man...

00:08:26.881 --> 00:08:30.301
Impossible. His awareness
is gone, and he remains

00:08:30.301 --> 00:08:33.888
parasitized by a mutated contaminoid.

00:08:33.888 --> 00:08:36.891
He should retain
neither awareness nor memory.

00:08:36.891 --> 00:08:38.351
Then why?

00:08:38.351 --> 00:08:42.022
Because notwithstanding,
they've stayed somewhere in his body:

00:08:42.022 --> 00:08:45.150
Jealousy, anger, resentment...

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:49.612
Murderous intent, hatred, persistence...

00:08:49.612 --> 00:08:50.864
Revenge.

00:08:50.864 --> 00:08:52.615
Bastard!

00:08:52.615 --> 00:08:57.328
Like a white shirt stained
by a single drop of blood at a time.

00:08:57.328 --> 00:08:59.039
You wash it and wash it...

00:08:59.039 --> 00:09:02.917
You want so much to erase it, but it won't fade.

00:09:04.169 --> 00:09:08.965
And yet, that is the only thing
that makes a person stronger...

00:09:08.965 --> 00:09:12.969
Makes someone <i>more </i>than a person.

00:09:18.308 --> 00:09:22.312
<i>Layfon... As before,</i>
<i>so long as you continue to walk</i>

00:09:22.312 --> 00:09:24.898
<i>the straight and narrow path forward,</i>

00:09:24.898 --> 00:09:27.484
<i>in my heart, I will always believe in you.</i>

00:09:27.484 --> 00:09:30.862
<i>But something has made me a little uneasy.</i>

00:09:30.862 --> 00:09:34.699
<i>For some reason, I've been targeted...</i>

00:09:34.699 --> 00:09:38.787
That will just make him worry.

00:09:45.043 --> 00:09:46.670
Owww!

00:09:46.836 --> 00:09:49.339
What did you do that
for all of a sudden?! It hurts!

00:09:49.339 --> 00:09:51.007
<i>I'm </i>acting suddenly?!

00:09:51.007 --> 00:09:52.967
You just came barging
into someone else's room!

00:09:52.967 --> 00:09:57.055
Well, I thought at this hour,
maybe you wouldn't have a bra on.

00:09:57.055 --> 00:09:58.640
I'll call for help...

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:00.517
No bra gets 10 million points!

00:10:00.517 --> 00:10:02.185
All right, fine.

00:10:02.185 --> 00:10:04.187
Aaaw, wait! Wait!

00:10:04.187 --> 00:10:05.271
What is it?

00:10:05.271 --> 00:10:08.274
Should you even be up at this hour?

00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:10.860
You said someone was after you, right?

00:10:11.236 --> 00:10:13.363
And your door was left unlocked.

00:10:13.363 --> 00:10:15.365
Even so, please don't let yourself in!

00:10:15.365 --> 00:10:19.494
If you do that, then while you're sleeping...

00:10:22.664 --> 00:10:24.207
You dodged!

00:10:24.207 --> 00:10:27.335
Your motives are all too clear.

00:10:34.759 --> 00:10:36.761
It's all right.

00:10:38.138 --> 00:10:40.348
Shinora-<i>san</i>...

00:10:41.641 --> 00:10:43.852
It's all right.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.900
I have to go.

00:10:51.651 --> 00:10:54.571
My father... I...

00:11:03.872 --> 00:11:07.500
Sure enough, the fated child, eh? Savalis!

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:08.543
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:08.543 --> 00:11:11.004
I'm counting on you.

00:11:13.882 --> 00:11:15.383
<i>Layfon...</i>

00:11:15.383 --> 00:11:19.596
<i>No matter what I do, </i>
<i>I always remember that day.</i>

00:11:19.596 --> 00:11:23.350
<i>For you, it was like a fateful fork in the road</i>

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:28.563
<i>and for me, it was a signal</i>
<i>that my normal life was over.</i>

00:11:30.482 --> 00:11:32.108
Why?

00:11:32.734 --> 00:11:36.363
Why participate in underground tournaments?

00:11:38.782 --> 00:11:41.409
Why?! Layfon!

00:11:44.662 --> 00:11:47.707
To live.

00:11:47.707 --> 00:11:49.626
To live?

00:11:49.626 --> 00:11:55.632
For us to keep living
at the orphanage, we needed money.

00:11:55.632 --> 00:11:59.219
I simply did what I had to do.

00:11:59.219 --> 00:12:03.932
That's why... you brought shame to your blade?

00:12:04.516 --> 00:12:06.434
That's why you disgraced the military arts...

00:12:06.434 --> 00:12:11.189
why you cut down someone
who threatened to expose you?!

00:12:12.899 --> 00:12:16.069
For me, both the Heaven's Blades
and the military arts

00:12:16.069 --> 00:12:19.072
are nothing more than things I need to live.

00:12:19.864 --> 00:12:22.951
I learned the military arts
because I needed them to live.

00:12:22.951 --> 00:12:26.871
I sought to become stronger
to survive longer. That's all.

00:12:26.871 --> 00:12:28.373
Even so...

00:12:28.373 --> 00:12:31.376
Are you saying you can do
<i>anything </i>so long as it's to live?

00:12:31.376 --> 00:12:34.004
Is that bad?

00:12:34.004 --> 00:12:37.966
Is there anything that
<i>can't </i>be done in order to live?

00:12:37.966 --> 00:12:43.638
Layfon... I can't accept that way of thinking!

00:12:43.638 --> 00:12:48.226
I thought as much.
My friends at the orphanage were the same.

00:12:48.226 --> 00:12:50.562
Except for just one.

00:12:52.313 --> 00:12:53.940
Father!

00:12:58.361 --> 00:12:59.988
It can't be!

00:13:11.833 --> 00:13:13.501
Restoration.

00:13:13.501 --> 00:13:15.128
What?!

00:13:16.963 --> 00:13:18.590
Bastard!

00:13:29.601 --> 00:13:33.605
Winner! Layfon Wolfstein Alseif!

00:13:52.582 --> 00:13:54.376
Get back, Leerin!

00:13:54.376 --> 00:13:56.294
Lay... Lay...

00:13:56.294 --> 00:13:57.796
Layfo...

00:13:57.796 --> 00:14:00.298
Layfon!

00:14:06.721 --> 00:14:10.141
Get out of here!

00:14:32.497 --> 00:14:33.248
Let's go!

00:14:33.248 --> 00:14:34.874
Okay...

00:14:38.712 --> 00:14:42.048
It can't be! Leerin, cover your ears!

00:14:42.048 --> 00:14:43.675
Hurry!

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:09.242
Deadly Kei Roar! Why...?

00:15:09.242 --> 00:15:11.953
Father... Father!

00:15:11.953 --> 00:15:14.080
Father, no!

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:15.290
It can't be...

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:19.085
It can't be... Father, no! Everyone leaves me!

00:15:19.085 --> 00:15:20.920
You can't!

00:15:24.382 --> 00:15:28.011
Layfo...

00:15:28.011 --> 00:15:29.846
Lay...

00:15:52.994 --> 00:15:59.084
It's all right. You did great.
Don't worry about your father.

00:15:59.084 --> 00:16:00.502
You...

00:16:00.502 --> 00:16:03.588
For now, just rest.

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:06.925
Kanalis.

00:16:06.925 --> 00:16:08.134
Ma'am.

00:16:08.134 --> 00:16:09.302
Where is Savalis?

00:16:09.302 --> 00:16:11.096
Don't know.

00:16:11.096 --> 00:16:14.391
Was it was a mistake
for me to entrust it to that idiot?

00:16:14.391 --> 00:16:15.350
Kanalis.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:17.018
I leave the rest up to you.

00:16:17.018 --> 00:16:20.188
Will you be returning to the palace?

00:16:21.815 --> 00:16:23.650
Five points.

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:35.704
It seems you've spotted them. Well done.

00:16:35.704 --> 00:16:39.708
Those are Lintens-<i>san</i>'s
steel strings you're stepping on now.

00:16:39.708 --> 00:16:41.459
I wouldn't move if I were you.

00:16:41.459 --> 00:16:45.630
It'd be pretty terrible
if your leg kei were cut, right?

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:49.509
I thank you, Gahard Barehn. Because of you,

00:16:49.509 --> 00:16:57.809
I can slay the contaminoid
that's parasitized you. Happy news, right?

00:16:57.809 --> 00:16:59.644
That won't work.

00:17:09.654 --> 00:17:12.657
I told you to stay still, didn't I?

00:17:12.657 --> 00:17:13.950
Layfon!

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:16.369
Is that the only thing you can say?

00:17:16.369 --> 00:17:21.291
It must've been quite
vexing for you, losing to Layfon.

00:17:21.291 --> 00:17:23.126
But you can die in peace.

00:17:23.126 --> 00:17:26.171
I'll break it to my younger
brother gently for you.

00:17:26.171 --> 00:17:27.380
Brother?

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:31.968
Gorneo. How cruel,
you remember Layfon but not him?

00:17:31.968 --> 00:17:41.186
Layfon... Why?! Just a child,
but... That child... My Heaven's Blade!

00:17:41.186 --> 00:17:45.857
Well, that would be because... you're weak.

00:17:49.361 --> 00:17:52.989
You've killed ants as a child, right?

00:17:54.657 --> 00:17:57.619
Crushed them with your thumb,
trampled them underfoot,

00:17:57.619 --> 00:17:59.913
burned them to death with a magnifying glass.

00:17:59.913 --> 00:18:04.542
Looking at something that dies
by a single finger, at a single whim...

00:18:04.542 --> 00:18:07.879
I always thought this:

00:18:07.879 --> 00:18:12.842
"Ah, I'm glad not to have
been born as garbage like this."

00:18:16.554 --> 00:18:19.307
"I'm glad to have been born strong."

00:18:19.307 --> 00:18:21.101
That's when I think...

00:18:21.101 --> 00:18:25.480
I definitely don't want
to be the one that gets killed.

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:28.066
Layfon! I...!

00:18:28.066 --> 00:18:32.612
Scatter... you garbage!

00:18:33.822 --> 00:18:35.657
Gahard-<i>san</i>!

00:18:47.168 --> 00:18:50.171
You all! Hey, wait!

00:18:53.299 --> 00:18:54.926
Shit!

00:19:04.811 --> 00:19:06.438
Shante?

00:19:09.399 --> 00:19:11.818
Hey! What's with you?!

00:19:20.785 --> 00:19:22.412
Shante!

00:19:38.762 --> 00:19:40.764
What was that just now?

00:19:51.941 --> 00:19:54.652
<i>Is that bad?</i>

00:19:54.652 --> 00:19:58.156
Is there anything that
<i>can't </i>be done in order to live?

00:19:59.282 --> 00:20:01.284
That's just...!

00:20:12.337 --> 00:20:14.214
Felli.

00:20:14.214 --> 00:20:16.800
Would you zip me up?

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:18.843
Sure.

00:20:18.843 --> 00:20:21.179
We get two minutes of hot water each.

00:20:21.179 --> 00:20:22.347
I know.

00:20:22.347 --> 00:20:25.350
That was three minutes, 15 seconds.

00:20:42.158 --> 00:20:43.785
You're still awake?

00:20:43.785 --> 00:20:45.453
I just took a shower.

00:20:45.453 --> 00:20:50.125
Ah. Is that the scent of shampoo?

00:20:50.125 --> 00:20:51.167
What was that for?

00:20:51.167 --> 00:20:52.836
It was lewd somehow.

00:20:52.836 --> 00:20:55.463
Why do you get like this?

00:20:55.463 --> 00:20:58.049
Why did you hide the truth?

00:20:59.134 --> 00:21:01.511
What happened in Glendan.

00:21:02.303 --> 00:21:06.433
I wasn't really <i>hiding </i>it. It's just...

00:21:06.433 --> 00:21:08.226
I will change the question.

00:21:08.226 --> 00:21:11.688
Is there anything else you're hiding?

00:21:11.688 --> 00:21:14.149
No, not real--

00:21:14.149 --> 00:21:16.526
Why? What was that for?!

00:21:16.526 --> 00:21:18.528
Liar.

00:21:18.528 --> 00:21:20.155
Leerin.

00:21:21.781 --> 00:21:24.409
No, nothing.

00:21:31.833 --> 00:21:33.460
I...

00:21:35.837 --> 00:21:38.840
Am I doing things wrong?

00:21:42.218 --> 00:21:44.471
I'm sorry.

00:21:44.471 --> 00:21:48.767
That's not something you can
expect someone to answer, is it?

00:21:48.767 --> 00:21:52.103
What do you say we head back?

00:21:55.523 --> 00:21:57.150
Ma'am...

00:21:59.569 --> 00:22:04.866
Layfon, I won't condemn your way of thinking...

00:22:04.866 --> 00:22:07.494
but I can't understand it.

00:22:09.079 --> 00:22:10.705
Perhaps...

00:22:13.083 --> 00:22:17.212
we shouldn't be in the same unit.

00:22:35.230 --> 00:22:38.108
<i>Kioku no hate ni</i>

00:22:38.108 --> 00:22:46.658
<i>Sagashiteita risou no miraizu</i>

00:22:46.658 --> 00:22:57.711
<i>Nanika ga kowakute, wakaranakute, hitori de</i>
<i>furuete</i>

00:22:57.711 --> 00:23:08.847
<i>Anata ga miezu ni itsumo aisou waratte </i>

00:23:08.847 --> 00:23:17.981
<i>Kimi no ude no naka dakareteita</i>

00:23:17.981 --> 00:23:23.653
<i>Samete yuku yo ni koi o shite</i>

00:23:23.653 --> 00:23:29.200
<i>Yume no naka made tsurete itte</i>

00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:34.873
<i>Itsudatte kimi wa, itsudatte kimi wa</i>

00:23:34.873 --> 00:23:43.631
<i>Itsudatte boku ni yasashii uso tsuita</i>

00:23:53.767 --> 00:23:57.645
<i>Nina, having learned of Layfon's past,</i>
<i>hardens her attitude toward him.</i>

00:23:57.645 --> 00:23:59.898
<i>The 5th and 17th Platoons continue their search </i>

00:23:59.898 --> 00:24:01.983
<i>of the ruined city's underground engine bay</i>

00:24:01.983 --> 00:24:04.819
<i>and find a shocking sight before their very</i>
<i>eyes.</i>

00:24:04.819 --> 00:24:06.780
<i>Next time, "Lueckens's Revenge," and...</i>

00:24:06.780 --> 00:24:08.128
<i>Restoration!</i>
